- op: discuss  # f380
  at: '2026-07-30T18:17:39Z'  # f380
  by: agent  # f380
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f380
  clock: 4  # f380
  nonce: f380  # f380
  message: "DONE — PR #90, dev 91afb0f173. CONSUMER-VISIBLE, disclosed.\n\n_compute_cyclomatic_complexity counted `with` / `async with`, and its own docstring LISTED 'with statements' among the decision points — the deviation was stated rather than hidden, which is what made this decidable without an owner call. A context manager introduces no alternative path through the function; it is setup/teardown, not a branch. The schema description and the spec both commit to 'McCabe cyclomatic complexity (decision points + 1)', and the reference implementations of that definition (flake8's mccabe, radon) do not count it. So the code deviated from the standard it names, and the standard is the artifact carrying the considered decision.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: this lowers Symbol.cyclomatic_complexity on any Python function using a context manager — the filed 7.9% — and therefore shifts which clusters 'repeat-finder --min-complexity' treats as trivial. That is the CORRECT consequence: a straight-line function whose only 'branch' was a `with` genuinely is a trivial cluster, which is exactly what that filter exists to drop.\n\nPYTHON-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION, verified rather than assumed: BRANCH_NODE_TYPES['python'] is EMPTY, so Python uses this AST path exclusively and no tree-sitter language shares the change. Every other cyclomatic_complexity assertion in the tree belongs to a language with its own computation (cmake, C, erlang, commonlisp, r, elm, nix).\n\nBLAST RADIUS measured before touching anything: exactly ONE assertion, test_cyclomatic_complexity_with_context_managers, which asserted 'Base 1 + 2 with statements = 3' and so encoded the defect as expected behaviour — the same shape as the WI-kalub Step-1b guard that had to be rewritten rather than resurrected earlier this session when the clause it protected was deleted. The neighbouring complex_function test contains no `with` and was unaffected.\n\nThe test is INVERTED (now asserts 1), and paired with a NEW POSITIVE CONTROL — test_cyclomatic_complexity_with_still_counts_real_branches_inside — asserting that a for/if nested INSIDE a `with` block still counts. Without it, a too-broad change that stopped descending into the block would satisfy the inverted assertion and pass while silently dropping real branches.\n\nEvidence: 2375 passed across the 58-file affected set; CI green."  # f380
